<h1>Team Communication &amp; Announcements</h1>

<p class="lead">Team announcement software that keeps messages scoped to the right teams, scheduled to appear and expire — so you’re not re-sending in five group chats.</p>

<img src="/images/ss-calendar.png" alt="Announcements feed showing team-scoped posts with scheduled publishing and email summary options" width="827" height="827" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;max-width:560px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;" class="rounded border">

<section id="overview" class="card" aria-labelledby="overview-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="overview-heading">Announcements that know who they’re for</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>GatherPack replaces reply-all threads with announcements tied to <a href="/features/members/">teams</a>. Post for a single team or the whole organization, schedule posts to appear and expire automatically, and keep important resources on content pages that are actually findable. Email summaries go out on a regular cadence so people who missed the feed still catch the highlights.</p>
    <p class="mb-0">If you live in Slack, Discord, or text, we hear you — those channels are <a href="/roadmap/">on the roadmap</a> as explicit integrations, not vague promises.</p>
  </div>
</section>

